## Monitoring Setup

### Azure Monitor Agent

Installed Azure Monitor Agent on `lab10-vm`.

```bash
az vm extension set \
  --resource-group "$RG" \
  --vm-name "$VM" \
  --name AzureMonitorLinuxAgent \
  --publisher Microsoft.Azure.Monitor \
  --version 1.0
```

### Data Collection Rule

Created `lab10-dcr` to collect Linux Syslog data and send it to `lab10-law`.

```text
VM Syslog
   ↓
Azure Monitor Agent
   ↓
DCR
   ↓
Log Analytics Workspace
```

The DCR was associated with `lab10-vm`.

### KQL

Basic queries were practiced, for example:

```kusto
Heartbeat
| where Computer == "lab10-vm"
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
| take 10
```

```kusto
Syslog
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
| take 20
```

Syslog generation on the VM was confirmed with:

```bash
logger "Lab10 test message"
```

However, the Syslog records did not appear in Log Analytics during the lab. This was recorded as a monitoring ingestion issue rather than expanding the lab into deeper AMA troubleshooting.

