# 5. Application ↔ Database Communication Failure

Created a second VM:

```text
DB VM
lab10-db-vm
10.10.0.5
```

Installed Docker and PostgreSQL 16.

PostgreSQL container:

```bash
sudo docker run -d \
  --name lab10-postgres \
  -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=Lab10Pass123! \
  -e POSTGRES_DB=lab10db \
  -p 5432:5432 \
  postgres:16
```

Verified the container:

```bash
sudo docker ps
```

The application VM tested connectivity to PostgreSQL:

```bash
nc -zv -w 5 10.10.0.5 5432
```

Initially:

```text
Connection to 10.10.0.5 5432 port [tcp/postgresql] succeeded!
```

### Intentional Failure

The DB VM's NSG initially had only an explicit SSH allow rule.

Communication between the two VMs was possible because they were in the same VNet and Azure's default `AllowVNetInBound` rule permits VNet traffic.

An intentional deny rule was then created:

```bash
az network nsg rule create \
  --resource-group "$RG" \
  --nsg-name "lab10-db-vmNSG" \
  --name "block-postgres-5432" \
  --priority 900 \
  --direction Inbound \
  --access Deny \
  --protocol Tcp \
  --source-address-prefixes 10.10.0.4 \
  --destination-port-ranges 5432
```

The connection test then failed:

```text
nc: connect to 10.10.0.5 port 5432 timed out
```

The NSG rules confirmed:

```text
block-postgres-5432
Priority: 900
Source: 10.10.0.4
Access: Deny
Protocol: Tcp
Destination Port: 5432
```

The deny rule was deleted:

```bash
az network nsg rule delete \
  --resource-group "$RG" \
  --nsg-name "lab10-db-vmNSG" \
  --name "block-postgres-5432"
```

Connectivity was restored:

```text
Connection to 10.10.0.5 5432 port [tcp/postgresql] succeeded!
```

### Learned

`5432` is the standard TCP port used by PostgreSQL.

The troubleshooting process demonstrated:

```text
Application → DB failure
        ↓
Check IP / destination
        ↓
Check TCP connectivity
        ↓
Check NSG
        ↓
Identify blocking rule
        ↓
Remove blocking rule
        ↓
Confirm connectivity restored
```

This demonstrated the difference between:

* Azure NSG network filtering
* VM networking
* Docker port mapping
* PostgreSQL service

